cy](https://foundation.rust-lang.org/policies/privacy-policy/#docs.rs)\n\n* [Rust](#)\n  * [Rust website](https://www.rust-lang.org/)\n  * [The Book](https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/)\n  * [Standard Library API Reference](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/)\n  * [Rust by Example](https://doc.rust-lang.org/rust-by-example/)\n  * [The Cargo Guide](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/)\n  * [Clippy Documentation](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/clippy)\n\n<iframe src=\"/-/storage-change-detection.html\" width=\"0\" height=\"0\" style=\"display: none\"></iframe>\n\n[nftables](../../nftables/index.html)0.6.3\n----------\n\n[Batch](#)\n----------\n\n### [Methods](#implementations) ###\n\n* [add](#method.add)\n* [add\\_all](#method.add_all)\n* [add\\_cmd](#method.add_cmd)\n* [add\\_obj](#method.add_obj)\n* [delete](#method.delete)\n* [new](#method.new)\n* [to\\_nftables](#method.to_nftables)\n\n### [Trait Implementations](#trait-implementations) ###\n\n* [Clone](#impl-Clone-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n* [Debug](#impl-Debug-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n* [Default](#impl-Default-for-Batch%3C'_%3E)\n* [Deserialize\\<'de\\>](#impl-Deserialize%3C'de%3E-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n* [Eq](#impl-Eq-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n* [PartialEq](#impl-PartialEq-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n* [Serialize](#impl-Serialize-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n* [StructuralPartialEq](#impl-StructuralPartialEq-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n\n### [Auto Trait Implementations](#synthetic-implementations) ###\n\n* [Freeze](#impl-Freeze-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n* [RefUnwindSafe](#impl-RefUnwindSafe-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n* [Send](#impl-Send-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n* [Sync](#impl-Sync-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n* [Unpin](#impl-Unpin-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n* [UnwindSafe](#impl-UnwindSafe-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n\n### [Blanket Implementations](#blanket-implementations) ###\n\n* [Any](#impl-Any-for-T)\n* [Borrow\\<T\\>](#impl-Borrow%3CT%3E-for-T)\n* [BorrowMut\\<T\\>](#impl-BorrowMut%3CT%3E-for-T)\n* [CloneToUninit](#impl-CloneToUninit-for-T)\n* [DeserializeOwned](#impl-DeserializeOwned-for-T)\n* [DynClone](#impl-DynClone-for-T)\n* [From\\<T\\>](#impl-From%3CT%3E-for-T)\n* [Into\\<U\\>](#impl-Into%3CU%3E-for-T)\n* [ToOwned](#impl-ToOwned-for-T)\n* [TryFrom\\<U\\>](#impl-TryFrom%3CU%3E-for-T)\n* [TryInto\\<U\\>](#impl-TryInto%3CU%3E-for-T)\n\n[In nftables::batch](index.html)\n----------\n\n[nftables](../index.html)::[batch](index.html)\n\nStruct BatchCopy item path\n==========\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#7-9)\n\n```\npub struct Batch<'a> { /* private fields */ }\n```\n\n<details class=\"toggle top-doc\" open=\"\"><summary class=\"hideme\">Expand description</summary>\n\nBatch manages nftables objects and is used to prepare an nftables payload.\n\n</details>\n\nImplementations[§](#implementations)\n----------\n\n<details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#17-55)[§](#impl-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Batch](struct.Batch.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#19-21)\n\n#### pub fn [new](#method.new)() -\\> [Batch](struct.Batch.html)\\<'a\\> ####\n\n</summary>\n\nCreates an empty Batch instance.\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#24-26)\n\n#### pub fn [add](#method.add)(&mut self, obj: [NfListObject](../schema/enum.NfListObject.html)\\<'a\\>) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nAdds object with `add` command to Batch.\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#29-31)\n\n#### pub fn [delete](#method.delete)(&mut self, obj: [NfListObject](../schema/enum.NfListObject.html)\\<'a\\>) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nAdds object with `delete` command to Batch.\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#34-36)\n\n#### pub fn [add\\_cmd](#method.add_cmd)(&mut self, cmd: [NfCmd](../schema/enum.NfCmd.html)\\<'a\\>) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nAdds a command to Batch.\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#40-42)\n\n#### pub fn [add\\_obj](#method.add_obj)(&mut self, obj: [NfListObject](../schema/enum.NfListObject.html)\\<'a\\>) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nAdds a list object (without a command) directly to Batch.\nThis corresponds to the descriptive output format of `nft -j list ruleset`.\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#45-47)\n\n#### pub fn [add\\_all](#method.add_all)\\<I: [IntoIterator](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/iter/traits/collect/trait.IntoIterator.html)\\<Item = [NfObject](../schema/enum.NfObject.html)\\<'a\\>\\>\\>(&mut self, objs: I) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nAdds all given objects to the batch.\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#50-54)\n\n#### pub fn [to\\_nftables](#method.to_nftables)(self) -\\> [Nftables](../schema/struct.Nftables.html)\\<'a\\> ####\n\n</summary>\n\nWraps Batch in nftables object.\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\nTrait Implementations[§](#trait-implementations)\n----------\n\n<details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#5)[§](#impl-Clone-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Clone](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.Clone.html) for [Batch](struct.Batch.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#5)[§](#method.clone)\n\n#### fn [clone](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.Clone.html#tymethod.clone)(&self) -\\> [Batch](struct.Batch.html)\\<'a\\> ####\n\n</summary>\n\nReturns a duplicate of the value. [Read more](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.Clone.html#tymethod.clone)\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n1.0.0 · [Source](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/src/core/clone.rs.html#246-248)[§](#method.clone_from)\n\n#### fn [clone\\_from](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.Clone.html#method.clone_from)(&mut self, source: &Self) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nPerforms copy-assignment from `source`. [Read more](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.Clone.html#method.clone_from)\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#5)[§](#impl-Debug-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Debug](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/trait.Debug.html) for [Batch](struct.Batch.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#5)[§](#method.fmt)\n\n#### fn [fmt](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/trait.Debug.html#tymethod.fmt)(&self, f: &mut [Formatter](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/struct.Formatter.html)\\<'\\_\\>) -\\> [Result](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/type.Result.html) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nFormats the value using the given formatter. [Read more](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/trait.Debug.html#tymethod.fmt)\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#11-15)[§](#impl-Default-for-Batch%3C'_%3E)\n\n### impl [Default](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/default/trait.Default.html) for [Batch](struct.Batch.html)\\<'\\_\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#12-14)[§](#method.default)\n\n#### fn [default](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/default/trait.Default.html#tymethod.default)() -\\> Self ####\n\n</summary>\n\nReturns the “default value” for a type. [Read more](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/default/trait.Default.html#tymethod.default)\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#5)[§](#impl-Deserialize%3C'de%3E-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'de, 'a\\> [Deserialize](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/de/trait.Deserialize.html)\\<'de\\> for [Batch](struct.Batch.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#5)[§](#method.deserialize)\n\n#### fn [deserialize](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/de/trait.Deserialize.html#tymethod.deserialize)\\<\\_\\_D\\>(\\_\\_deserializer: \\_\\_D) -\\> [Result](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/result/enum.Result.html)\\<Self, \\_\\_D::[Error](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/de/trait.Deserializer.html#associatedtype.Error)\\>\n\nwhere \\_\\_D: [Deserializer](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/de/trait.Deserializer.html)\\<'de\\>,\n\n ####\n\n</summary>\n\nDeserialize this value from the given Serde deserializer. [Read more](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/de/trait.Deserialize.html#tymethod.deserialize)\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#5)[§](#impl-PartialEq-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [PartialEq](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/trait.PartialEq.html) for [Batch](struct.Batch.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#5)[§](#method.eq)\n\n#### fn [eq](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/trait.PartialEq.html#tymethod.eq)(&self, other: &[Batch](struct.Batch.html)\\<'a\\>) -\\> [bool](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.bool.html) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nTests for `self` and `other` values to be equal, and is used by `==`.\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n1.0.0 · [Source](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/src/core/cmp.rs.html#265)[§](#method.ne)\n\n#### fn [ne](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/trait.PartialEq.html#method.ne)(&self, other: [&Rhs](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.reference.html)) -\\> [bool](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.bool.html) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nTests for `!=`. The default implementation is almost always sufficient,\nand should not be overridden without very good reason.\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#5)[§](#impl-Serialize-for-Batch%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Serialize](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serialize.html) for [Batch](struct.Batch.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/batch.rs.html#5)[§](#method.serialize)\n\n#### fn [serialize](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serialize.html#tymethod.serialize)\\<\\_\\_S\\>(&self, \\_\\_serializer: \\_\\_S) -\\> [Result](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/result/enum.Result.html)\\<\\_\\_S::[Ok](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serializer.html#associatedtype.Ok), \\_\\_S::[Error](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serializer.html#associatedtype.Error)\\>\n\nwhere \\_\\_S: [Serializer](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serializer.html),\n\n ####\n\n</summary>\n\nSerialize this value into the given Serde serializer. [Read more](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serialize.html#tymethod.serialize)\n\n</details>\n\n</detail