vacy policy](https://foundation.rust-lang.org/policies/privacy-policy/#docs.rs)\n\n* [Rust](#)\n  * [Rust website](https://www.rust-lang.org/)\n  * [The Book](https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/)\n  * [Standard Library API Reference](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/)\n  * [Rust by Example](https://doc.rust-lang.org/rust-by-example/)\n  * [The Cargo Guide](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/)\n  * [Clippy Documentation](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/clippy)\n\n<iframe src=\"/-/storage-change-detection.html\" width=\"0\" height=\"0\" style=\"display: none\"></iframe>\n\n[nftables](../../nftables/index.html)0.6.3\n----------\n\n[Statement](#)\n----------\n\n### [Variants](#variants) ###\n\n* [Accept](#variant.Accept)\n* [CTCount](#variant.CTCount)\n* [CTExpectation](#variant.CTExpectation)\n* [CTHelper](#variant.CTHelper)\n* [CTTimeout](#variant.CTTimeout)\n* [Continue](#variant.Continue)\n* [Counter](#variant.Counter)\n* [DNAT](#variant.DNAT)\n* [Drop](#variant.Drop)\n* [Dup](#variant.Dup)\n* [FWD](#variant.FWD)\n* [Flow](#variant.Flow)\n* [Goto](#variant.Goto)\n* [Jump](#variant.Jump)\n* [Limit](#variant.Limit)\n* [Log](#variant.Log)\n* [Mangle](#variant.Mangle)\n* [Masquerade](#variant.Masquerade)\n* [Match](#variant.Match)\n* [Meter](#variant.Meter)\n* [Notrack](#variant.Notrack)\n* [Queue](#variant.Queue)\n* [Quota](#variant.Quota)\n* [Redirect](#variant.Redirect)\n* [Reject](#variant.Reject)\n* [Return](#variant.Return)\n* [SNAT](#variant.SNAT)\n* [Set](#variant.Set)\n* [SynProxy](#variant.SynProxy)\n* [TProxy](#variant.TProxy)\n* [VerdictMap](#variant.VerdictMap)\n* [XT](#variant.XT)\n\n### [Trait Implementations](#trait-implementations) ###\n\n* [Clone](#impl-Clone-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n* [Debug](#impl-Debug-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n* [Deserialize\\<'de\\>](#impl-Deserialize%3C'de%3E-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n* [Eq](#impl-Eq-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n* [JsonSchema](#impl-JsonSchema-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n* [PartialEq](#impl-PartialEq-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n* [Serialize](#impl-Serialize-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n* [StructuralPartialEq](#impl-StructuralPartialEq-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n\n### [Auto Trait Implementations](#synthetic-implementations) ###\n\n* [Freeze](#impl-Freeze-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n* [RefUnwindSafe](#impl-RefUnwindSafe-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n* [Send](#impl-Send-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n* [Sync](#impl-Sync-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n* [Unpin](#impl-Unpin-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n* [UnwindSafe](#impl-UnwindSafe-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n\n### [Blanket Implementations](#blanket-implementations) ###\n\n* [Any](#impl-Any-for-T)\n* [Borrow\\<T\\>](#impl-Borrow%3CT%3E-for-T)\n* [BorrowMut\\<T\\>](#impl-BorrowMut%3CT%3E-for-T)\n* [CloneToUninit](#impl-CloneToUninit-for-T)\n* [DeserializeOwned](#impl-DeserializeOwned-for-T)\n* [DynClone](#impl-DynClone-for-T)\n* [From\\<T\\>](#impl-From%3CT%3E-for-T)\n* [Into\\<U\\>](#impl-Into%3CU%3E-for-T)\n* [ToOwned](#impl-ToOwned-for-T)\n* [TryFrom\\<U\\>](#impl-TryFrom%3CU%3E-for-T)\n* [TryInto\\<U\\>](#impl-TryInto%3CU%3E-for-T)\n\n[In nftables::stmt](index.html)\n----------\n\n[nftables](../index.html)::[stmt](index.html)\n\nEnum StatementCopy item path\n==========\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#20-89)\n\n```\n#[non_exhaustive]pub enum Statement<'a> {\nShow 32 variants    Accept(Option<Accept>),\n    Drop(Option<Drop>),\n    Continue(Option<Continue>),\n    Return(Option<Return>),\n    Jump(JumpTarget<'a>),\n    Goto(JumpTarget<'a>),\n    Match(Match<'a>),\n    Counter(Counter<'a>),\n    Mangle(Mangle<'a>),\n    Quota(QuotaOrQuotaRef<'a>),\n    Limit(Limit<'a>),\n    Flow(Flow<'a>),\n    FWD(Option<FWD<'a>>),\n    Notrack,\n    Dup(Dup<'a>),\n    SNAT(Option<NAT<'a>>),\n    DNAT(Option<NAT<'a>>),\n    Masquerade(Option<NAT<'a>>),\n    Redirect(Option<NAT<'a>>),\n    Reject(Option<Reject>),\n    Set(Set<'a>),\n    Log(Option<Log<'a>>),\n    CTHelper(Cow<'a, str>),\n    Meter(Meter<'a>),\n    Queue(Queue<'a>),\n    VerdictMap(VerdictMap<'a>),\n    CTCount(CTCount<'a>),\n    CTTimeout(Expression<'a>),\n    CTExpectation(Expression<'a>),\n    XT(Option<Value>),\n    SynProxy(SynProxy),\n    TProxy(TProxy<'a>),\n}\n```\n\n<details class=\"toggle top-doc\" open=\"\"><summary class=\"hideme\">Expand description</summary>\n\nStatements are the building blocks for rules. Each rule consists of at least one.\n\nSee [https://manpages.debian.org/testing/libnftables1/libnftables-json.5.en.html#STATEMENTS](https://manpages.debian.org/testing/libnftables1/libnftables-json.5.en.html#STATEMENTS).\n\n</details>\n\nVariants (Non-exhaustive)[§](#variants)\n----------\n\n<details class=\"toggle non-exhaustive\"><summary class=\"hideme\">This enum is marked as non-exhaustive</summary>\n\nNon-exhaustive enums could have additional variants added in future. Therefore, when matching against variants of non-exhaustive enums, an extra wildcard arm must be added to account for any future variants.\n\n</details>\n\n[§](#variant.Accept)\n\n### Accept([Option](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/option/enum.Option.html)\\<[Accept](struct.Accept.html)\\>) ###\n\n`accept` verdict.\n\n[§](#variant.Drop)\n\n### Drop([Option](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/option/enum.Option.html)\\<[Drop](struct.Drop.html)\\>) ###\n\n`drop` verdict.\n\n[§](#variant.Continue)\n\n### Continue([Option](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/option/enum.Option.html)\\<[Continue](struct.Continue.html)\\>) ###\n\n`continue` verdict.\n\n[§](#variant.Return)\n\n### Return([Option](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/option/enum.Option.html)\\<[Return](struct.Return.html)\\>) ###\n\n`return` verdict.\n\n[§](#variant.Jump)\n\n### Jump([JumpTarget](struct.JumpTarget.html)\\<'a\\>) ###\n\n`jump` verdict. Expects a target chain name.\n\n[§](#variant.Goto)\n\n### Goto([JumpTarget](struct.JumpTarget.html)\\<'a\\>) ###\n\n`goto` verdict. Expects a target chain name.\n\n[§](#variant.Match)\n\n### Match([Match](struct.Match.html)\\<'a\\>) ###\n\n[§](#variant.Counter)\n\n### Counter([Counter](enum.Counter.html)\\<'a\\>) ###\n\nanonymous or named counter.\n\n[§](#variant.Mangle)\n\n### Mangle([Mangle](struct.Mangle.html)\\<'a\\>) ###\n\n[§](#variant.Quota)\n\n### Quota([QuotaOrQuotaRef](enum.QuotaOrQuotaRef.html)\\<'a\\>) ###\n\nanonymous or named quota.\n\n[§](#variant.Limit)\n\n### Limit([Limit](struct.Limit.html)\\<'a\\>) ###\n\n[§](#variant.Flow)\n\n### Flow([Flow](struct.Flow.html)\\<'a\\>) ###\n\nThe Flow statement offloads matching network traffic to flowtables,\nenabling faster forwarding by bypassing standard processing.\n\n[§](#variant.FWD)\n\n### FWD([Option](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/option/enum.Option.html)\\<[FWD](struct.FWD.html)\\<'a\\>\\>) ###\n\n[§](#variant.Notrack)\n\n### Notrack ###\n\nDisable connection tracking for the packet.\n\n[§](#variant.Dup)\n\n### Dup([Dup](struct.Dup.html)\\<'a\\>) ###\n\n[§](#variant.SNAT)\n\n### SNAT([Option](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/option/enum.Option.html)\\<[NAT](struct.NAT.html)\\<'a\\>\\>) ###\n\n[§](#variant.DNAT)\n\n### DNAT([Option](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/option/enum.Option.html)\\<[NAT](struct.NAT.html)\\<'a\\>\\>) ###\n\n[§](#variant.Masquerade)\n\n### Masquerade([Option](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/option/enum.Option.html)\\<[NAT](struct.NAT.html)\\<'a\\>\\>) ###\n\n[§](#variant.Redirect)\n\n### Redirect([Option](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/option/enum.Option.html)\\<[NAT](struct.NAT.html)\\<'a\\>\\>) ###\n\n[§](#variant.Reject)\n\n### Reject([Option](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/option/enum.Option.html)\\<[Reject](struct.Reject.html)\\>) ###\n\n[§](#variant.Set)\n\n### Set([Set](struct.Set.html)\\<'a\\>) ###\n\n[§](#variant.Log)\n\n### Log([Option](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/option/enum.Option.html)\\<[Log](struct.Log.html)\\<'a\\>\\>) ###\n\n[§](#variant.CTHelper)\n\n### CTHelper([Cow](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/borrow/enum.Cow.html)\\<'a, [str](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.str.html)\\>) ###\n\nEnable the specified conntrack helper for this packet.\n\n[§](#variant.Meter)\n\n### Meter([Meter](struct.Meter.html)\\<'a\\>) ###\n\n[§](#variant.Queue)\n\n### Queue([Queue](struct.Queue.html)\\<'a\\>) ###\n\n[§](#variant.VerdictMap)\n\n### VerdictMap([VerdictMap](struct.VerdictMap.html)\\<'a\\>) ###\n\n[§](#variant.CTCount)\n\n### CTCount([CTCount](struct.CTCount.html)\\<'a\\>) ###\n\n[§](#variant.CTTimeout)\n\n### CTTimeout([Expression](../expr/enum.Expression.html)\\<'a\\>) ###\n\nAssign connection tracking timeout policy.\n\n[§](#variant.CTExpectation)\n\n### CTExpectation([Expression](../expr/enum.Expression.html)\\<'a\\>) ###\n\nAssign connection tracking expectation.\n\n[§](#variant.XT)\n\n### XT([Option](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/option/enum.Option.html)\\<[Value](https://docs.rs/serde_json/1.0.142/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde_json/value/enum.Value.html)\\>) ###\n\nThis represents an xt statement from xtables compat interface.\nSadly, at this point, it is not possible to provide any further information about its content.\n\n[§](#variant.SynProxy)\n\n### SynProxy([SynProxy](struct.SynProxy.html)) ###\n\nA netfilter synproxy intercepts new TCP connections and handles the initial 3-way handshake using syncookies instead of conntrack to establish the connection.\n\n[§](#variant.TProxy)\n\n### TProxy([TProxy](struct.TProxy.html)\\<'a\\>) ###\n\nRedirects the packet to a local socket without changing the packet header in any way.\n\nTrait Implementations[§](#trait-implementations)\n----------\n\n<details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#14)[§](#impl-Clone-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Clone](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.Clone.html) for [Statement](enum.Statement.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#14)[§](#method.clone)\n\n#### fn [clone](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.Clone.html#tymethod.clone)(&self) -\\> [Statement](enum.Statement.html)\\<'a\\> ####\n\n</summary>\n\nReturns a duplicate of the value. [Read more](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.Clone.html#tymethod.clone)\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n1.0.0 · [Source](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/src/core/clone.rs.html#246-248)[§](#method.clone_from)\n\n#### fn [clone\\_from](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.Clone.html#method.clone_from)(&mut self, source: &Self) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nPerforms copy-assignment from `source`. [Read more](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.Clone.html#method.clone_from)\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#14)[§](#impl-Debug-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Debug](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/trait.Debug.html) for [Statement](enum.Statement.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#14)[§](#method.fmt)\n\n#### fn [fmt](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/trait.Debug.html#tymethod.fmt)(&self, f: &mut [Formatter](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/struct.Formatter.html)\\<'\\_\\>) -\\> [Result](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/type.Result.html) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nFormats the value using the given formatter. [Read more](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/trait.Debug.html#tymethod.fmt)\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#14)[§](#impl-Deserialize%3C'de%3E-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'de, 'a\\> [Deserialize](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/de/trait.Deserialize.html)\\<'de\\> for [Statement](enum.Statement.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#14)[§](#method.deserialize)\n\n#### fn [deserialize](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/de/trait.Deserialize.html#tymethod.deserialize)\\<\\_\\_D\\>(\\_\\_deserializer: \\_\\_D) -\\> [Result](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/result/enum.Result.html)\\<Self, \\_\\_D::[Error](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/de/trait.Deserializer.html#associatedtype.Error)\\>\n\nwhere \\_\\_D: [Deserializer](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/de/trait.Deserializer.html)\\<'de\\>,\n\n ####\n\n</summary>\n\nDeserialize this value from the given Serde deserializer. [Read more](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/de/trait.Deserialize.html#tymethod.deserialize)\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#14)[§](#impl-JsonSchema-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [JsonSchema](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html) for [Statement](enum.Statement.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#14)[§](#method.schema_name)\n\n#### fn [schema\\_name](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html#tymethod.schema_name)() -\\> [Cow](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/borrow/enum.Cow.html)\\<'static, [str](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.str.html)\\> ####\n\n</summary>\n\nThe name of the generated JSON Schema. [Read more](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html#tymethod.schema_name)\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#14)[§](#method.schema_id)\n\n#### fn [schema\\_id](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html#method.schema_id)() -\\> [Cow](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/borrow/enum.Cow.html)\\<'static, [str](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.str.html)\\> ####\n\n</summary>\n\nReturns a string that uniquely identifies the schema produced by this type. [Read more](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html#method.schema_id)\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#14)[§](#method.json_schema)\n\n#### fn [json\\_schema](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html#tymethod.json_schema)(generator: &mut [SchemaGenerator](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/generate/struct.SchemaGenerator.html)) -\\> [Schema](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/schema/struct.Schema.html) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nGenerates a JSON Schema for this type. [Read more](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html#tymethod.json_schema)\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#14)[§](#method.inline_schema)\n\n#### fn [inline\\_schema](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html#method.inline_schema)() -\\> [bool](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.bool.html) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nWhether JSON Schemas generated for this type should be included directly in parent schemas,\nrather than being re-used where possible using the `$ref` keyword. [Read more](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html#method.inline_schema)\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#14)[§](#impl-PartialEq-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [PartialEq](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/trait.PartialEq.html) for [Statement](enum.Statement.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#14)[§](#method.eq)\n\n#### fn [eq](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/trait.PartialEq.html#tymethod.eq)(&self, other: &[Statement](enum.Statement.html)\\<'a\\>) -\\> [bool](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.bool.html) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nTests for `self` and `other` values to be equal, and is used by `==`.\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n1.0.0 · [Source](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/src/core/cmp.rs.html#265)[§](#method.ne)\n\n#### fn [ne](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/trait.PartialEq.html#method.ne)(&self, other: [&Rhs](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.reference.html)) -\\> [bool](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.bool.html) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nTests for `!=`. The default implementation is almost always sufficient,\nand should not be overridden without very good reason.\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#14)[§](#impl-Serialize-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Serialize](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serialize.html) for [Statement](enum.Statement.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#14)[§](#method.serialize)\n\n#### fn [serialize](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serialize.html#tymethod.serialize)\\<\\_\\_S\\>(&self, \\_\\_serializer: \\_\\_S) -\\> [Result](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/result/enum.Result.html)\\<\\_\\_S::[Ok](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serializer.html#associatedtype.Ok), \\_\\_S::[Error](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serializer.html#associatedtype.Error)\\>\n\nwhere \\_\\_S: [Serializer](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serializer.html),\n\n ####\n\n</summary>\n\nSerialize this value into the given Serde serializer. [Read more](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serialize.html#tymethod.serialize)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#14)[§](#impl-Eq-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Eq](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/trait.Eq.html) for [Statement](enum.Statement.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#14)[§](#impl-StructuralPartialEq-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [StructuralPartialEq](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/marker/trait.StructuralPartialEq.html) for [Statement](enum.Statement.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\nAuto Trait Implementations[§](#synthetic-implementations)\n----------\n\n[§](#impl-Freeze-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Freeze](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/marker/trait.Freeze.html) for [Statement](enum.Statement.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n[§](#impl-RefUnwindSafe-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [RefUnwindSafe](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/panic/unwind_safe/trait.RefUnwindSafe.html) for [Statement](enum.Statement.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n[§](#impl-Send-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Send](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/marker/trait.Send.html) for [Statement](enum.Statement.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n[§](#impl-Sync-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Sync](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/marker/trait.Sync.html) for [Statement](enum.Statement.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n[§](#impl-Unpin-for-Statement%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Unpin](https://doc.rust-lang.