ttps://foundation.rust-lang.org/policies/privacy-policy/#docs.rs)\n\n* [Rust](#)\n  * [Rust website](https://www.rust-lang.org/)\n  * [The Book](https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/)\n  * [Standard Library API Reference](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/)\n  * [Rust by Example](https://doc.rust-lang.org/rust-by-example/)\n  * [The Cargo Guide](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/)\n  * [Clippy Documentation](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/clippy)\n\n<iframe src=\"/-/storage-change-detection.html\" width=\"0\" height=\"0\" style=\"display: none\"></iframe>\n\n[nftables](../../nftables/index.html)0.6.3\n----------\n\n[Counter](#)\n----------\n\n### [Variants](#variants) ###\n\n* [Anonymous](#variant.Anonymous)\n* [Named](#variant.Named)\n\n### [Trait Implementations](#trait-implementations) ###\n\n* [Clone](#impl-Clone-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n* [Debug](#impl-Debug-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n* [Deserialize\\<'de\\>](#impl-Deserialize%3C'de%3E-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n* [Eq](#impl-Eq-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n* [JsonSchema](#impl-JsonSchema-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n* [PartialEq](#impl-PartialEq-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n* [Serialize](#impl-Serialize-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n* [StructuralPartialEq](#impl-StructuralPartialEq-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n\n### [Auto Trait Implementations](#synthetic-implementations) ###\n\n* [Freeze](#impl-Freeze-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n* [RefUnwindSafe](#impl-RefUnwindSafe-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n* [Send](#impl-Send-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n* [Sync](#impl-Sync-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n* [Unpin](#impl-Unpin-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n* [UnwindSafe](#impl-UnwindSafe-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n\n### [Blanket Implementations](#blanket-implementations) ###\n\n* [Any](#impl-Any-for-T)\n* [Borrow\\<T\\>](#impl-Borrow%3CT%3E-for-T)\n* [BorrowMut\\<T\\>](#impl-BorrowMut%3CT%3E-for-T)\n* [CloneToUninit](#impl-CloneToUninit-for-T)\n* [DeserializeOwned](#impl-DeserializeOwned-for-T)\n* [DynClone](#impl-DynClone-for-T)\n* [From\\<T\\>](#impl-From%3CT%3E-for-T)\n* [Into\\<U\\>](#impl-Into%3CU%3E-for-T)\n* [ToOwned](#impl-ToOwned-for-T)\n* [TryFrom\\<U\\>](#impl-TryFrom%3CU%3E-for-T)\n* [TryInto\\<U\\>](#impl-TryInto%3CU%3E-for-T)\n\n[In nftables::stmt](index.html)\n----------\n\n[nftables](../index.html)::[stmt](index.html)\n\nEnum CounterCopy item path\n==========\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#129-134)\n\n```\npub enum Counter<'a> {\n    Named(Cow<'a, str>),\n    Anonymous(Option<AnonymousCounter>),\n}\n```\n\n<details class=\"toggle top-doc\" open=\"\"><summary class=\"hideme\">Expand description</summary>\n\nAnonymous or named Counter.\n\n</details>\n\nVariants[§](#variants)\n----------\n\n[§](#variant.Named)\n\n### Named([Cow](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/borrow/enum.Cow.html)\\<'a, [str](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.str.html)\\>) ###\n\nA counter referenced by name.\n\n[§](#variant.Anonymous)\n\n### Anonymous([Option](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/option/enum.Option.html)\\<[AnonymousCounter](struct.AnonymousCounter.html)\\>) ###\n\nAn anonymous counter.\n\nTrait Implementations[§](#trait-implementations)\n----------\n\n<details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#126)[§](#impl-Clone-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Clone](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.Clone.html) for [Counter](enum.Counter.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#126)[§](#method.clone)\n\n#### fn [clone](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.Clone.html#tymethod.clone)(&self) -\\> [Counter](enum.Counter.html)\\<'a\\> ####\n\n</summary>\n\nReturns a duplicate of the value. [Read more](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.Clone.html#tymethod.clone)\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n1.0.0 · [Source](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/src/core/clone.rs.html#246-248)[§](#method.clone_from)\n\n#### fn [clone\\_from](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.Clone.html#method.clone_from)(&mut self, source: &Self) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nPerforms copy-assignment from `source`. [Read more](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.Clone.html#method.clone_from)\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#126)[§](#impl-Debug-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Debug](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/trait.Debug.html) for [Counter](enum.Counter.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#126)[§](#method.fmt)\n\n#### fn [fmt](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/trait.Debug.html#tymethod.fmt)(&self, f: &mut [Formatter](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/struct.Formatter.html)\\<'\\_\\>) -\\> [Result](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/type.Result.html) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nFormats the value using the given formatter. [Read more](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/fmt/trait.Debug.html#tymethod.fmt)\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#126)[§](#impl-Deserialize%3C'de%3E-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'de, 'a\\> [Deserialize](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/de/trait.Deserialize.html)\\<'de\\> for [Counter](enum.Counter.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#126)[§](#method.deserialize)\n\n#### fn [deserialize](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/de/trait.Deserialize.html#tymethod.deserialize)\\<\\_\\_D\\>(\\_\\_deserializer: \\_\\_D) -\\> [Result](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/result/enum.Result.html)\\<Self, \\_\\_D::[Error](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/de/trait.Deserializer.html#associatedtype.Error)\\>\n\nwhere \\_\\_D: [Deserializer](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/de/trait.Deserializer.html)\\<'de\\>,\n\n ####\n\n</summary>\n\nDeserialize this value from the given Serde deserializer. [Read more](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/de/trait.Deserialize.html#tymethod.deserialize)\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#126)[§](#impl-JsonSchema-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [JsonSchema](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html) for [Counter](enum.Counter.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#126)[§](#method.schema_name)\n\n#### fn [schema\\_name](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html#tymethod.schema_name)() -\\> [Cow](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/borrow/enum.Cow.html)\\<'static, [str](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.str.html)\\> ####\n\n</summary>\n\nThe name of the generated JSON Schema. [Read more](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html#tymethod.schema_name)\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#126)[§](#method.schema_id)\n\n#### fn [schema\\_id](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html#method.schema_id)() -\\> [Cow](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/borrow/enum.Cow.html)\\<'static, [str](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.str.html)\\> ####\n\n</summary>\n\nReturns a string that uniquely identifies the schema produced by this type. [Read more](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html#method.schema_id)\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#126)[§](#method.json_schema)\n\n#### fn [json\\_schema](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html#tymethod.json_schema)(generator: &mut [SchemaGenerator](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/generate/struct.SchemaGenerator.html)) -\\> [Schema](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/schema/struct.Schema.html) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nGenerates a JSON Schema for this type. [Read more](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html#tymethod.json_schema)\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#126)[§](#method.inline_schema)\n\n#### fn [inline\\_schema](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html#method.inline_schema)() -\\> [bool](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.bool.html) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nWhether JSON Schemas generated for this type should be included directly in parent schemas,\nrather than being re-used where possible using the `$ref` keyword. [Read more](https://docs.rs/schemars/1.0.4/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/schemars/trait.JsonSchema.html#method.inline_schema)\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#126)[§](#impl-PartialEq-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [PartialEq](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/trait.PartialEq.html) for [Counter](enum.Counter.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#126)[§](#method.eq)\n\n#### fn [eq](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/trait.PartialEq.html#tymethod.eq)(&self, other: &[Counter](enum.Counter.html)\\<'a\\>) -\\> [bool](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.bool.html) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nTests for `self` and `other` values to be equal, and is used by `==`.\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n1.0.0 · [Source](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/src/core/cmp.rs.html#265)[§](#method.ne)\n\n#### fn [ne](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/trait.PartialEq.html#method.ne)(&self, other: [&Rhs](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.reference.html)) -\\> [bool](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.bool.html) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nTests for `!=`. The default implementation is almost always sufficient,\nand should not be overridden without very good reason.\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#126)[§](#impl-Serialize-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Serialize](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serialize.html) for [Counter](enum.Counter.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#126)[§](#method.serialize)\n\n#### fn [serialize](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serialize.html#tymethod.serialize)\\<\\_\\_S\\>(&self, \\_\\_serializer: \\_\\_S) -\\> [Result](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/result/enum.Result.html)\\<\\_\\_S::[Ok](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serializer.html#associatedtype.Ok), \\_\\_S::[Error](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serializer.html#associatedtype.Error)\\>\n\nwhere \\_\\_S: [Serializer](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serializer.html),\n\n ####\n\n</summary>\n\nSerialize this value into the given Serde serializer. [Read more](https://docs.rs/serde/1.0.219/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/serde/ser/trait.Serialize.html#tymethod.serialize)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#126)[§](#impl-Eq-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Eq](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/trait.Eq.html) for [Counter](enum.Counter.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n[Source](../../src/nftables/stmt.rs.html#126)[§](#impl-StructuralPartialEq-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [StructuralPartialEq](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/marker/trait.StructuralPartialEq.html) for [Counter](enum.Counter.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\nAuto Trait Implementations[§](#synthetic-implementations)\n----------\n\n[§](#impl-Freeze-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Freeze](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/marker/trait.Freeze.html) for [Counter](enum.Counter.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n[§](#impl-RefUnwindSafe-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [RefUnwindSafe](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/panic/unwind_safe/trait.RefUnwindSafe.html) for [Counter](enum.Counter.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n[§](#impl-Send-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Send](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/marker/trait.Send.html) for [Counter](enum.Counter.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n[§](#impl-Sync-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Sync](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/marker/trait.Sync.html) for [Counter](enum.Counter.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n[§](#impl-Unpin-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [Unpin](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/marker/trait.Unpin.html) for [Counter](enum.Counter.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\n[§](#impl-UnwindSafe-for-Counter%3C'a%3E)\n\n### impl\\<'a\\> [UnwindSafe](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/panic/unwind_safe/trait.UnwindSafe.html) for [Counter](enum.Counter.html)\\<'a\\> ###\n\nBlanket Implementations[§](#blanket-implementations)\n----------\n\n<details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\"><summary>\n\n[Source](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/src/core/any.rs.html#138)[§](#impl-Any-for-T)\n\n### impl\\<T\\> [Any](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/any/trait.Any.html) for T\n\nwhere T: 'static + ?[Sized](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/marker/trait.Sized.html),\n\n ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/src/core/any.rs.html#139)[§](#method.type_id)\n\n#### fn [type\\_id](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/any/trait.Any.html#tymethod.type_id)(&self) -\\> [TypeId](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/any/struct.TypeId.html) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nGets the `TypeId` of `self`. [Read more](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/any/trait.Any.html#tymethod.type_id)\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\"><summary>\n\n[Source](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/src/core/borrow.rs.html#209)[§](#impl-Borrow%3CT%3E-for-T)\n\n### impl\\<T\\> [Borrow](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/borrow/trait.Borrow.html)\\<T\\> for T\n\nwhere T: ?[Sized](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/marker/trait.Sized.html),\n\n ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/src/core/borrow.rs.html#211)[§](#method.borrow)\n\n#### fn [borrow](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/borrow/trait.Borrow.html#tymethod.borrow)(&self) -\\> [&T](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.reference.html) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nImmutably borrows from an owned value. [Read more](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/borrow/trait.Borrow.html#tymethod.borrow)\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\"><summary>\n\n[Source](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/src/core/borrow.rs.html#217)[§](#impl-BorrowMut%3CT%3E-for-T)\n\n### impl\\<T\\> [BorrowMut](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/borrow/trait.BorrowMut.html)\\<T\\> for T\n\nwhere T: ?[Sized](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/marker/trait.Sized.html),\n\n ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/src/core/borrow.rs.html#218)[§](#method.borrow_mut)\n\n#### fn [borrow\\_mut](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/borrow/trait.BorrowMut.html#tymethod.borrow_mut)(&mut self) -\\> [&mut T](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.reference.html) ####\n\n</summary>\n\nMutably borrows from an owned value. [Read more](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/borrow/trait.BorrowMut.html#tymethod.borrow_mut)\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\"><summary>\n\n[Source](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/src/core/clone.rs.html#516)[§](#impl-CloneToUninit-for-T)\n\n### impl\\<T\\> [CloneToUninit](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.CloneToUninit.html) for T\n\nwhere T: [Clone](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.Clone.html),\n\n ###\n\n</summary>\n\n<details class=\"toggle method-toggle\" open=\"\"><summary>\n\n[Source](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/src/core/clone.rs.html#518)[§](#method.clone_to_uninit)\n\n#### unsafe fn [clone\\_to\\_uninit](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.CloneToUninit.html#tymethod.clone_to_uninit)(&self, dest: [\\*mut ](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.pointer.html)[u8](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.u8.html)) ####\n\n</summary>\n\n🔬This is a nightly-only experimental API. (`clone_to_uninit`)\n\nPerforms copy-assignment from `self` to `dest`. [Read more](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.CloneToUninit.html#tymethod.clone_to_uninit)\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details class=\"toggle implementors-toggle\"><summary>\n\n[Source](https://docs.rs/dyn-clone/1.0.20/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/src/dyn_clone/lib.rs.html#196-198)[§](#impl-DynClone-for-T)\n\n### impl\\<T\\> [DynClone](https://docs.rs/dyn-clone/1.0.20/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/dyn_clone/trait.DynClone.html) for T\n\nwhere T: [Clone](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/clone/trait.Clone.html