t-lang.org/book/)\n  * [Standard Library API Reference](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/)\n  * [Rust by Example](https://doc.rust-lang.org/rust-by-example/)\n  * [The Cargo Guide](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/)\n  * [Clippy Documentation](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/clippy)\n\n gloo-timers 0.3.0\n==========\n\nConvenience crate for working with JavaScript timers\n\n* [ Crate ](/crate/gloo-timers/latest)\n* [ Source ](/crate/gloo-timers/latest/source/)\n* [ Builds ](/crate/gloo-timers/latest/builds)\n* [Feature flags ](/crate/gloo-timers/latest/features)\n\n[ Documentation ](/gloo-timers/latest/gloo_timers/)\n\n* Coverage\n* **100%**  \n  **16** out of **16** items documented**11** out of **14** items with examples\n* Size\n* Source code size: 30.33 kB This is the summed size of all the files inside the crates.io package for this release.\n* Documentation size: 2.37 MB This is the summed size of all files generated by rustdoc for all configured targets\n* Links\n* [ Homepage ](https://github.com/rustwasm/gloo)\n* [ Repository](https://github.com/rustwasm/gloo/tree/master/crates/timers)\n* [ crates.io ](https://crates.io/crates/gloo-timers)\n* Dependencies\n* * [ futures-channel ^0.3 *normal* *optional* ](/crate/futures-channel/^0.3)\n  * [ futures-core ^0.3 *normal* *optional* ](/crate/futures-core/^0.3)\n  * [ js-sys ^0.3.31 *normal* ](/crate/js-sys/^0.3.31)\n  * [ wasm-bindgen ^0.2 *normal* ](/crate/wasm-bindgen/^0.2)\n  * [ futures-util ^0.3 *dev* ](/crate/futures-util/^0.3)\n  * [ wasm-bindgen-futures ^0.4.4 *dev* ](/crate/wasm-bindgen-futures/^0.4.4)\n  * [ wasm-bindgen-test ^0.3.4 *dev* ](/crate/wasm-bindgen-test/^0.3.4)\n\n* Versions\n* * [**0.3.0** (2023-08-11)](/crate/gloo-timers/0.3.0)\n  * [**0.2.6** (2023-01-21)](/crate/gloo-timers/0.2.6)\n  * [**0.2.5** (2022-11-29)](/crate/gloo-timers/0.2.5)\n  * [**0.2.4** (2022-04-13)](/crate/gloo-timers/0.2.4)\n  * [**0.2.3** (2022-01-28)](/crate/gloo-timers/0.2.3)\n  * [**0.2.2** (2021-12-05)](/crate/gloo-timers/0.2.2)\n  * [**0.2.1** (2020-03-11)](/crate/gloo-timers/0.2.1)\n  * [**0.2.0** (2019-12-12)](/crate/gloo-timers/0.2.0)\n  * [**0.1.0** (2019-09-13)](/crate/gloo-timers/0.1.0)\n\n* Owners\n* [![alexcrichton](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64996?v=4) ](https://crates.io/users/alexcrichton)[ ![ashleygwilliams](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1163554?v=4) ](https://crates.io/users/ashleygwilliams)[ ![fitzgen](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74571?v=4) ](https://crates.io/users/fitzgen)[ ![Pauan](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97238?v=4) ](https://crates.io/users/Pauan)[ ![github:rustwasm:core](https://avatars1.githubusercontent.com/u/37272798?v=4) ](https://crates.io/users/github:rustwasm:core)[ ![jstarry](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1076145?v=4) ](https://crates.io/users/jstarry)[ ![ranile](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47357913?v=4) ](https://crates.io/users/ranile)\n\nBuilt with 🦀🕸 by The Rust and WebAssembly Working Group\n\nWorking with timers on the Web: `setTimeout` and `setInterval`.\n\nThese APIs come in two flavors:\n\n1. a callback style (that more directly mimics the JavaScript APIs), and\n2. a `Future`s and `Stream`s API.\n\n### Timeouts ###\n\nTimeouts fire once after a period of time (measured in milliseconds).\n\n#### Timeouts with a Callback Function ####\n\n```\nuse gloo_timers::callback::Timeout;\n\nlet timeout = Timeout::new(1_000, move || {\n    // Do something after the one second timeout is up!\n});\n\n// Since we don't plan on cancelling the timeout, call `forget`.\ntimeout.forget();\n\n```\n\n#### Timeouts as `Future`s ####\n\nWith the `futures` feature enabled, a `future` module containing futures-based\ntimers is exposed.","type":"text"}]}}
